libdrm is the userspace library for the kernel's DRM/KMS graphics interface, which
compositors and mesa use to drive displays and GPUs. Built with the AMD backends
(radeon, amdgpu) and the generic core; Intel, nouveau and the embedded SoC drivers
are off for now. Installs libdrm*, headers and .pc files under /usr/local.
upstream: https://dri.freedesktop.org/libdrm/
